    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:c3205ac1e20a266d",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "7bb8c45a65f39f006fd083247acf433245c643c5224f34bffeec3a4219c229c0",
      "text": "Day 9 · After breakfast, a 9-hour excursion to Viña del Mar and Valparaíso, through the olive groves, orchards and vineyards of the Curacaví and Casablanca valleys (120 km from Santiago). Built on 42 hills, Valparaíso is famous for its architecture and listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site, its levels linked by historic funiculars, stairways and footpaths. Visit Sotomayor Square and the Naval Headquarters, a national monument, then walk to Cerro Concepción along the Gervasoni and Atkinson promenades, with a magnificent view over the port. Continue to Viña del Mar, the “Garden City”, with its beautiful beaches and dramatic rocks: the Flower Clock, Reñaca Beach, the waterfront and the Fonck Museum. Stop for lunch, then return to Santiago.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1nHB-5Xavr6R_fNkR408Fk_Ch8G6c2l00",
        "documentSha256": "f30e74c88d9ecd8c21cebe8c69f0e733dd98d406ac3056d25ae9d00ef819452c",
